<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Open the simulator panel</h3>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-list--spaced">
  <li>Open the companion web app at the <code>CompanionUrl</code> output and add <code>?step=3</code> to the URL.</li>
  <li>The right-hand photo upload simulator pane brightens; the left and middle panes dim.</li>
  <li>In the sender-phone field, enter the same number you dialled from in Step 1. Use UK E.164 (<code>+44</code> followed by 10 digits) or local format (<code>0</code> followed by 10 digits). Cases looks up open tickets by phone number.</li>
  <li>Click "Attach photo" and choose any photo of a bin, fly-tip, or pothole. The repository includes <a href="https://github.com/co-cddo/ndx_try_aws_scenarios/tree/main/cloudformation/scenarios/ai-contact-centre/spikes/multimodal-fixtures" class="govuk-link">test fixtures</a> if you need one.</li>
  <li>Click "Send".</li>
</ol>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">What you'll see</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">A staged sequence of chat bubbles appears in the simulator pane:</p>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li><strong>~1 second:</strong> "Photo received. Sender ID: {your phone}"</li>
  <li><strong>~3 seconds:</strong> "Analysing image with Amazon Bedrock…" with a shimmer animation</li>
  <li><strong>~6 seconds:</strong> "Looking up your case in Connect Cases…"</li>
  <li><strong>~10 seconds:</strong> A structured response with <code>object_class</code>, <code>condition</code>, <code>severity</code>, <code>suggested_council_action</code>, <code>confidence</code>, and optional <code>secondary_observations</code></li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">Behind the scenes, the web app calls <code>POST /api/upload-presign</code> on the companion API. The browser uploads the image directly to S3 using a presigned URL. Then the web app calls <code>POST /api/simulator/send</code> with the S3 key and your phone number, and a Lambda function handles the cross-channel link to your existing case.</p>
